-- Fixture for the `l4 export --to=dmn --fail-on` threshold tests: a DMN
-- report that is blocking-ONLY (2 blocking, 0 lossy, 0 advisory).
--
-- Two formula decisions over one ASSUMEd input: each is a boxed literal
-- expression (D-LITERALEXPR, Blocking) and nothing else fires — no MAYBE, no
-- rename, no fixture, no regulative body. (This role used to be played by
-- export-two-rules.l4's two regulative decides, until Phase 4's population
-- filter correctly routed uncalled regulative bodies out of the DRG.)

ASSUME x IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A NUMBER
`twice x` MEANS x TIMES 2

GIVETH A NUMBER
`thrice x` MEANS x TIMES 3
